Z||000025||Phil||08-16-2000||06:34 AM||||Aren't HP and torque always equal at 5252 RPM?||||reg||1
Z||000026||HYPTNOTiSE||08-16-2000||07:24 AM||||yes phil they are.  HP is a function of torque and speed. Someone correct me if i'm wrong but...<P>Torque x speed/5250 = HP<P>SO every dyno print out has to cross at 5250. that's where torque and hp are always, always, always equal.<P>Everything's correct except for the formula could be wrong, I'm not exactly positive, but it's along those lines.||||reg||1
